+// WindowPoolMiB is the window pool a process gets on a server with this much
+// RAM (engine.SmuxWindowPool, set at start): 1/128 of RAM, 16 to 128 MiB.
+// A window past engine.SmuxNeedStreamBuffer takes from it what it needs (16
+// MiB at most: one connection at ~670 Mbit/s at 100 ms, 220 at 300 ms takes
+// 14), so a server carries several such connections at once each way, and
+// the others get the window they would have got without it.
+func WindowPoolMiB(ramMB int) int {
+	return min(max(ramMB/128, 16), 128)
+}
